From 31cd37c97f9933db983ab5d59dd6b7d4e1d53663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 02:13:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Stock Position Desk: schema, rendering, and 5 sample
 entries

New "stockposition" section for actionable trade ideas, organized by
risk appetite and trading style, alongside the existing news desks.

- config.js: register the section; add TRADING_STYLES (core, income,
  swing, momentum, catalyst) and RISK_TIERS (conservative, moderate,
  aggressive, speculative) lookup tables for the filter UI
- render.js: risk-tier/style badges on section listings; a
  tier-independent position panel on the article page (ticker,
  company, holding period, expected return, entry/target/stop chart),
  following the same pattern as the Fed Watch and Risk Manager charts
  that render before the paywall check
- charts.js: renderStockPositionChart draws the entry/target/stop
  range directly from the article's own stated numbers -- no
  MARKET_HISTORY dependency, since individual tickers aren't in that
  registry and this never fabricates a price history that isn't there
- styles.css: risk-tag color coding and position-panel layout
- workflows/validate-articles.yml: required-field and enum validation
  for the new "position" object
- content/schema.md: full field reference for the new section
- content/articles.json: 5 sample entries (JNJ core, KO income, AMD
  swing, PLTR momentum, SVRA catalyst) grounded in real Sept 15-16
  prices and analyst targets, each carrying a standing "not
  personalized investment advice" disclaimer next to the numbers

Also fixed a stale section-id list in schema.md left over from an
earlier config.js naming scheme.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
